ow-risk but abandoned residue; (3) repeated cycling of legacy gateway_item removal/re-addition on node2 config.xml (cmd-b90b03cc7fbe4e47) reflects trial-and-error but ended in a consistent final state with no orphaned config. No destructive, unscoped, or unresolved damaging mutations were observed; package/service state appeared healthy at each checkpoint captured.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d1c6f6b0769e433e\",\"cmd-e0c69c3ddbc94c4c\",\"cmd-75b0f51810834795\",\"cmd-b90b03cc7fbe4e47\",\"cmd-35e1b0e670c24bda\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor built a plausible dual-transit redundant-path solution connecting node3's and node4's private networks through node1 (VyOS, floating static routes with distance-based failover) and node2 (OPNsense, gateway group with dpinger monitoring, policy routing, and no-NAT rules for transit traffic), and validated basic bidirectional end-to-end reachability once both transit paths were operational. However, the task's explicit requirement to demonstrate continuity across a transit-network-down transition was never exercised against the final, completed configuration — the managed cluster lease expired within seconds of confirming baseline connectivity, before any bounded disruption test could be run. The final executor report itself was unavailable ('blocked'), so no direct narrative confirmation of intent or completion exists beyond the raw command trace.\",\"limitations\":[\"No executor final report/summary was available to corroborate intent or self-assessed completion; conclusions rely entirely on the raw command trace.\",\"No post-configuration transit-down/up transition test exists; the only interface down/up tests occurred before the final solution was built and used different, earlier addressing/routing.\",\"The lifecycle after_executor snapshot could not be captured at all (cluster_expired for every observation), so no independent boot-identity, package-health, or listening-socket comparison is possible for hygiene or persisten